.TH "CLIPHIST-DAEMON.SH" "1" "November 2026" "arran4/dotfiles" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
cliphist\-daemon.sh \- manage clipboard watchers for a Hyprland instance
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
\fBcliphist\-daemon.sh\fR
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Start wl\-paste clipboard watchers feeding cliphist. Use an instance\-specific lock and PID directory under XDG_RUNTIME_DIR (with a per\-user /tmp fallback), and restart only watchers matching the expected executable path. Typically launched by desktop configuration rather than interactively.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
\fBHYPRLAND_INSTANCE_SIGNATURE\fR
Scopes the managed watcher processes; defaults to default outside Hyprland.
.TP
\fBXDG_RUNTIME_DIR\fR
Preferred directory for per\-instance PID and lock state.
.SH REQUIREMENTS
Requires Bash, wl-paste, cliphist, flock, readlink, a writable runtime
directory and a Wayland clipboard session. Chezmoi resolves the
executable paths at template rendering time.
.SH LIFECYCLE
The helper takes a per-instance file lock, examines text.pid and
image.pid, and checks /proc/PID/exe before terminating a recorded
watcher. This prevents killing unrelated processes solely on the
basis of a reused PID. It starts separate text and image clipboard
watchers, both feeding cliphist store. Re-running the helper
restarts the watchers for the same Hyprland instance.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
cliphist-daemon.sh
ls "$XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/wl-paste/$HYPRLAND_INSTANCE_SIGNATURE"
.fi
.SH PRIVACY AND TROUBLESHOOTING
PID and lock state lives below XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/wl-paste/<instance>,
or a per-user /tmp fallback. If history stops updating, inspect this
directory and verify wl-paste and cliphist are installed. This
command does not clear clipboard history; copied secrets may remain
in the history managed by cliphist.
.SH SEE ALSO
hyprland\-keys(7)
